WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.222
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.522 --> 00:00:09.153
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.453 --> 00:00:14.473
Unit fourteen: Can / Can't (ability). Today you will say what you can and cannot do.

4
00:00:14.773 --> 00:00:17.507
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:21.862
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.717 --> 00:00:23.520
Can.

7
00:00:24.517 --> 00:00:26.667
Can means to be able to do something.

8
00:00:27.283 --> 00:00:28.401
I can swim.

9
00:00:29.017 --> 00:00:31.356
Your turn. Say: Can.

10
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:34.876
Can.

11
00:00:35.617 --> 00:00:36.467
Can't.

12
00:00:37.483 --> 00:00:39.460
Can't means not able to do something.

13
00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.283
She can't drive.

14
00:00:41.883 --> 00:00:44.338
Your turn. Say: Can't.

15
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:47.888
Can't.

16
00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:49.674
Ability.

17
00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:53.728
Ability means the power or skill to do something.

18
00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:55.782
Swimming is an ability.

19
00:00:56.383 --> 00:00:58.850
Your turn. Say: Ability.

20
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:02.573
Ability.

21
00:01:03.317 --> 00:01:04.132
Swim.

22
00:01:05.117 --> 00:01:07.093
Swim means to move through water.

23
00:01:07.683 --> 00:01:09.242
Fish swim in the river.

24
00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:12.293
Your turn. Say: Swim.

25
00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:15.937
Swim.

26
00:01:16.683 --> 00:01:17.348
Cook.

27
00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:20.442
Cook means to prepare food with heat.

28
00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:22.550
My mother can cook well.

29
00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.477
Your turn. Say: Cook.

30
00:01:28.333 --> 00:01:29.056
Cook.

31
00:01:29.817 --> 00:01:30.667
Speak.

32
00:01:31.683 --> 00:01:33.578
Speak means to talk with words.

33
00:01:34.183 --> 00:01:35.753
I can speak English.

34
00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:38.387
Your turn. Say: Speak.

35
00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:42.165
Speak.

36
00:01:42.917 --> 00:01:43.767
Possible.

37
00:01:44.783 --> 00:01:47.166
Possible means able to happen or be done.

38
00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.819
It is possible to learn quickly.

39
00:01:50.417 --> 00:01:53.139
Your turn. Say: Possible.

40
00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:56.931
Possible.

41
00:01:57.683 --> 00:01:58.882
Impossible.

42
00:01:59.883 --> 00:02:02.858
Impossible means not able to happen or be done.

43
00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.252
Flying alone is impossible.

44
00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.665
Your turn. Say: Impossible.

45
00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:12.687
Impossible.

46
00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.116
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:21.276
Visal, what can you do well? Tell me one thing.

48
00:02:22.383 --> 00:02:31.923
I can swim and I can cook. We use can to talk about ability. The verb after can is always the base verb: I can swim, not I can swims.

49
00:02:33.017 --> 00:02:34.575
And for things you cannot do?

50
00:02:35.683 --> 00:02:45.182
We say can't or cannot. I can't drive. She can't swim. It means that it is not possible for me. Can't is the short form of cannot.

51
00:02:46.283 --> 00:02:47.853
How do we ask a question?

52
00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:59.595
Put can first: Can you speak English? Yes, I can. No, I can't. The word order is can, then the subject, then the base verb.

53
00:03:00.733 --> 00:03:02.466
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:03.317 --> 00:03:06.233
Grammar focus: Can and can't plus base verb.

55
00:03:06.533 --> 00:03:07.755
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:10.171
I can swim very well.

57
00:03:11.083 --> 00:03:12.665
She can't drive a car.

58
00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:14.876
Can you speak English?

59
00:03:15.833 --> 00:03:23.353
Use can for ability and can't for no ability. After can, use the base verb with no s. Questions: Can you…?

60
00:03:24.117 --> 00:03:27.791
Be careful! Don't say: She can swims very well.

61
00:03:29.733 --> 00:03:31.942
Say: She can swim very well.

62
00:03:32.242 --> 00:03:34.311
Use the base verb after can.

63
00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.520
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:39.497
What Can You Do?.

65
00:03:39.797 --> 00:03:42.110
I can swim, and I can cook rice.

66
00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.529
My sister can speak English and French.

67
00:03:46.533 --> 00:03:49.229
She can't drive a car, because she is only twelve.

68
00:03:50.233 --> 00:03:52.862
Can you play the guitar? No, I can't.

69
00:03:53.867 --> 00:03:56.586
Many things are possible if you practise.

70
00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:01.702
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:04.410
He blank swim very fast.

72
00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:08.201
A, can. B, cans. C, is can.

73
00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:13.650
The answer is A: can.

74
00:04:14.817 --> 00:04:17.434
I blank drive a car. I am too young.

75
00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:21.504
A, can. B, can't. C, cannot to.

76
00:04:25.067 --> 00:04:26.811
The answer is B: can't.

77
00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:29.694
Which sentence is correct?

78
00:04:29.994 --> 00:04:34.402
A, She can sings.. B, She can sing.. C, She can to sing..

79
00:04:37.967 --> 00:04:40.291
The answer is B: She can sing..

80
00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:43.324
Can you cook? blank

81
00:04:43.624 --> 00:04:48.044
A, Yes, I can.. B, Yes, I do.. C, Yes, I cooks..

82
00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.122
The answer is A: Yes, I can..

83
00:04:55.283 --> 00:04:58.072
According to the reading, who speaks English and French?

84
00:04:58.372 --> 00:05:02.386
A, my sister. B, my brother. C, my mother.

85
00:05:05.933 --> 00:05:07.782
The answer is A: my sister.

86
00:05:08.967 --> 00:05:12.200
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:15.885
Write two things you can do and two things you can't do.

88
00:05:24.683 --> 00:05:26.102
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:26.402 --> 00:05:39.161
I can swim and I can cook rice. I can't drive a car and I can't play the piano. I use can for things I am able to do and can't for things I am not able to do. The verb after can stays the same.

90
00:05:39.461 --> 00:05:41.263
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:46.904
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and can and can't plus base verb.

92
00:05:47.204 --> 00:05:51.435
Today's value is self-awareness. Know your strengths and keep growing.

93
00:05:51.735 --> 00:05:54.387
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

94
00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:57.235
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

